cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, cite the authors, software title, version, repository
  URL, and exact commit used. Cite the associated research article separately
  when its bibliographic details are available. No publication or software DOI
  has been assigned in this metadata.
type: software
title: "Void-Guided Particle Packing (VGPP) for Two-Dimensional Periodic RVE Generation: MATLAB Implementation"
authors:
  - family-names: "Hashemi Soudmand"
    given-names: "Behzad"
  - family-names: "Mohsenzadeh"
    given-names: "Rasool"
version: "0.3.1-preview"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bsoudmand/VGPP-Periodic-RVE-Generation"
url: "https://github.com/bsoudmand/VGPP-Periodic-RVE-Generation"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB research implementation of Void-Guided Particle Packing for
  two-dimensional periodic disk configurations intended for particulate RVE
  studies. The consolidated workflow includes a monodisperse, fixed-final-radius
  VGPP/RSA-PBC benchmark, geometric auditing, spatial statistics, checkpoints,
  and archived-reference comparison routines. Full validation of the
  consolidated code in MATLAB R2024b remains outstanding; complete manuscript
  reproducibility is not claimed.
keywords:
  - "Void-Guided Particle Packing"
  - "periodic boundary conditions"
  - "representative volume elements"
  - "particulate microstructures"
  - "MATLAB"
  - "random sequential adsorption"
